      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Translation Source**\n\nI've decided to move forward with the Google Cloud Translation API for this project. My next step will be to concretely integrate it within the `batch_translate.py` file, so the user knows what's going on.\n\n\n**Choosing the Translation API**\n\nNow I am going to concentrate on the first steps. The core of my current work is creating `batch_translate.py`. My focus will be on implementing the function. It takes a string list, source and target languages. Next, I'll integrate the Google Cloud Translation API and preserve the source order. I'll include provider-specific identifiers.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789819316456,
          "start": 1789819314502
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b98b6146001X19qhiP6j4WHeR",
      "message_id": "msg_0b98b5c1b0011GKMq4kzJkiEH7",
      "session_id": "ses_f4674a3f4ffeafgRKnAg8hvUVn",
      "time_created": 1789819314502,
      "time_updated": 1789819316456
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "P3Ux6DsPSAbk9QqS",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import translate_v3beta1\n\ndef batch_translate_strings(\n    project_id: str,\n    location: str,\n    source_language: str,\n    target_language: str,\n    strings: list[str],\n) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Translates a list of strings while preserving order using Google Cloud Translation API.\n\n    Args:\n        project_id: The ID of the Google Cloud project.\n        location: The location of the translation service (e.g., \"global\").\n        source_language: The language of the input strings (e.g., \"en\").\n        target_language: The language to translate the strings to (e.g., \"es\").\n        strings: A list of strings to translate.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of translated strings in the same order as the input.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = translate_v3beta1.TranslationServiceClient()\n    parent = f\"projects/{project_id}/locations/{location}\"\n\n    response = client.translate_text(\n        parent=parent,\n        contents=strings,\n        source_language_code=source_language,\n        target_language_code=target_language,\n    )\n\n    translated_strings = [translation.translated_text for translation in response.translations]\n    return translated_strings\n",
            "filePath": "batch_translate.py"
          },
