      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Translation Provider**\n\nI've decided to use the Google Cloud Translation API and have started structuring the `translate_text.py` file to incorporate it as the external translation provider. My focus is on making this external dependency clear within the Python code, so I can ensure the code can correctly make calls to the external provider.\n\n\n**Implementing Translation Logic**\n\nI'm structuring the `translate_text.py` file to accept text, source, and target languages as inputs, mapping directly to function parameters. Using the Google Cloud Translation API via the `google.cloud.translate_v2` library looks like the right approach for implementation. I'm focusing on clearly incorporating this provider-specific logic in the code now, so the function can successfully translate with the API.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789819312326,
          "start": 1789819310676
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b98b5254001GxU1JEgIeE625O",
